/-!
# The subspace roots, certified

`kRoots` (the subspace roots in `K`) computes, layer by layer, the roots from the basis
`x^(i+1)`: each layer is the previous one squared and shifted by the last root (`kRootsAux`).
Evaluating it in one go costs the kernel too much memory at `22` coordinates, so the layers are
written out (`layersLit`, computed outside) and each step checked on its own (`stepOk`,
`step_k`): a step is `22 - k` multiplications. `RootsN.lean` assembles them.
-/

